-- title:
--   Residual Hecke eigensystem on the full Hecke algebra at level N
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the elements fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, assumed absolutely irreducible (the base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$). Let $S_0\subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S$, and $N\geq 1$ an integer whose prime divisors all lie in $S$ and outside $S_0$, with $p^2\nmid N$; assume $\bar\rho$ is unramified at each $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$, $q\nmid N$ (every element of an inertia subgroup at a valuation subring lying over $q$ acts as the identity); for each prime $q\neq p$ with $q\Vert N$, that $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and inertia at $q$ acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for each prime $q\neq p$ with $q^2\mid N$, that inertia at $q$ acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; and, if $p\mid N$, that $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. for each valuation subring over $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule $L$ spanned by a member of a basis, stable under the decomposition group, with $\bar\rho(\sigma)v-v\in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in inertia. Assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are $\mathbb{C}$-spanned by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients, and let $\theta:\mathbb{T}^S\to k$ be a ring homomorphism on the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{T}^S=$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of that space generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\theta':\mathbb{T}^{S_0}\to k$ on the (larger) algebra attached to $S_0$ such that: $\theta'$ restricted along the inclusion $\mathbb{T}^S\subseteq\mathbb{T}^{S_0}$ is $\theta$; for every prime $\ell\neq p$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$, $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$; $\theta'(U_q)=0$ for every prime $q\notin S_0$ with $q^2\mid N$; for every prime $q\notin S_0$ with $q\Vert N$, every valuation subring $P$ over $q$, every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $q$ for $P$, and every $k$-endomorphism $E$ of the inertia coinvariants $V/\sum_{\tau\in I_P}\mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$, one has $\theta'(U_q)=\mathrm{tr}(E)$; and, in case $p\nmid N$ and $p\notin S_0$, the same description holds at $p$ with $\theta'(T_p)=\mathrm{tr}(E)$ for $E$ induced by a Frobenius at $p$ on the inertia coinvariants at $p$.
--
--   This is the determination of the residual Hecke eigensystem cut out by $\bar\rho$ at a level of the given type: the eigensystem away from $S$ is extended to the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell\in S\setminus S_0$, $\ell\nmid N$) and $U_q$ ($q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$), the new values being read off from $\bar\rho$ via Frobenius traces on inertia coinvariants, with $U_q=0$ at the primes with $q^2\mid N$. It supplies the maximal ideal of the full Hecke algebra used in the modularity-lifting step, and is cited in the construction of the local Hecke algebra and of its corner ring.
-- source:
